Package: normpipe
Type: Package
Title: Population-Referenced Norms with Two Layers of Uncertainty for Any Questionnaire
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Johannes", "Zimmermann", email = "jz@uni-kassel.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description: Derives norm tables for self-report questionnaires from a
    weighted reference sample or from published frequency tables. An
    instrument is described in a configuration file (items with their
    response categories and values, versions and scales, the groups for
    which norms are tabulated, the norm scale); the pipeline then produces
    weighted percentile ranks and standard scores (T by default) per group
    with credible bands from a Bayesian bootstrap under a Dirichlet prior
    over the attainable scores, kernel norms along a continuous variable
    such as age, score-conditional and integrated intervals for the
    individual from calibrated graded response and bifactor models, and
    several export formats. An optional transfer module projects scales that
    the reference sample did not answer from bridge items, using donor
    samples and Bayesian distributional regression.
